<h1>direct chaining</h1>
<p>
(data structure)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
A <a href="collisionres.html"><em>collision resolution scheme</em></a> in which the <a href="hashtab.html"><em>hash table</em></a> is an <a href="array.html"><em>array</em></a> of <a href="link.html"><em>links</em></a> to <a href="list.html"><em>lists</em></a>. Each list holds all the items with the same hash value.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Generalization</strong> (I am a kind of ...)<br>
<a href="separateChaining.html"><em>separate chaining</em></a>.
</p>
<p>
<strong>Aggregate parent</strong> (I am a part of or used in ...)<br>
<a href="hashtab.html"><em>hash table</em></a>.
</p>
<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="linearSearch.html"><em>linear search</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
The items in the list may be searched and maintained with any list search algorithms. Any searchable data structure may be used instead of a list. </p> 
<p> After <a href="../terms.html#GBY91">[GBY91, pages 71-74]</a></em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>
<h2>Implementation</h2>
<a href="https://users.dcc.uchile.cl/~rbaeza/handbook/algs/3/3310.ins.c" target="_blank">insert (C)</a>, <a href="https://users.dcc.uchile.cl/~rbaeza/handbook/algs/3/3310.srch.c" target="_blank">search (C)</a>. Duane A. Bailey's <a href="http://www.cs.williams.edu/~bailey/JavaStructures/doc/structure/structure/ChainedHashtable.html" target="_blank">ChainedHashtable class</a> documentation in the <a href="http://www.cs.williams.edu/~bailey/JavaStructures/Software.html" target="_blank">structure package (Java)</a> from  <a href="http://www.cs.williams.edu/~bailey/JavaStructures/" target="_blank">Java Structures</a>: Data Structures in Java, for the Principled Programmer.

